    },
    "message": "Place tests by scope and guard the layout\n\nNew tests go to tests/unit/<owner>/, tests/integration/ or tests/e2e/ by\nthe widest scope they touch, named after the module, feature or user flow\nrather than a bug or a development round. Existing top-level files move\nwhen they are next changed. A repo test fails on new top-level files,\nmisplaced test files, or live_api markers outside tests/live. pytest uses\nimportlib import mode so scope directories can share file names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
